# Netlify-style redirects.
#
# IMPORTANT: This is the SPA fallback. The 200 status means "show this content
# but keep the URL as requested" -- so deep links like /services/facelift work.
#
# AFTER prerendering: each route has its own dist/<route>/index.html, which
# Netlify will serve directly (more specific match wins). This catch-all only
# fires for routes NOT in dist (e.g., 404s, future client-only routes).

# API routes must come BEFORE the catch-all: _redirects is evaluated ahead of
# netlify.toml, so its /api/* rule never fires if /* swallows the path first.
/api/*    /.netlify/functions/:splat    200

/*    /index.html   200
